    "user_request_original": "Design a periodic multilayer stack on fused_silica substrate with air incidence. Stack topology: 14 repeated pairs of hfo2 and SiO2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) (28 layers total), starting with hfo2 adjacent to air. Initial layer thicknesses: hfo2 at 75 nm, SiO2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) at 125 nm (quarter-wave optical thickness at 300 nm center wavelength). Optimization variables: scale factor applied uniformly to all layer thicknesses (range 0.8-1.2), and individual thickness adjustments per layer type within ±20% of scaled baseline. Evaluate performance at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Wavelength bands: 200-400 nm (maximize reflectance), 800-1500 nm (maximize transmittance). Material refractive indices from measured datasets for hfo2 and SiO2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos). Total layer count fixed at 28.",
